    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d490">

                <pb facs="0802" n="792" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg792"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to Lieutenant General Alvan C. Gillem,
                        Jr. </hi><anchor n="52" xml:id="d490-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-04-25">25 April 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>567. Pl[ea]s[e] give me up to date statement on US shipping being used for water
                    movement Chinese forces northward including phasing out of these ships due to
                    redeployment and also your estimate as to capability of any Chinese Agency
                    taking over after redeployment how many LSTs will be available in period June to
                    August inclusive.</p>
                <p>New subject: While I was in Washington the Navy Dept authorized the retention by
                        CinCPac<anchor n="53" xml:id="d490-f2"/> of Navy crew specialists,
                    approximately 2,000, would you pls find out from Admiral Cooke<anchor n="54"
                        xml:id="d490-f3"/> what the status of this is in China.</p>
                <pb facs="0803" n="793" xml:id="pg793"/>
                <p>New subject: Pls give me summary of repatriations shipping which might possibly
                    be used for further Chinese Troop movements, together with your estimated list
                    of dates of availability. Also give me state of shipment of supplies, combat,
                    food and other to Manchuria and prospective shipments or shipping possibilities
                    over next 6 months.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d490-f1" n="52" type="source" xml:id="d490-f1-content">
                <p>Acting Commanding General, U. S. Forces, China Theater, during the absence of
                    General Wedemeyer.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d490-f2" n="53" xml:id="d490-f2-content">
                <p>Commander in Chief, Pacific.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d490-f3" n="54" xml:id="d490-f3-content">
                <p>Vice Adm. Charles M. Cooke, Jr., Commander, U. S. 7th Fleet.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
